Implement user story AMSD-2041: [GO, UP, MX] Live Preview of Content in CMS

## Story Description
Original Requirements (discovery)  AS a Content Author, I WANT to preview draft entries in CMS, SO THAT I can see how content will be shown on the website
ability to preview draft entries in CMS
Notes& Assumptions  Limitation: Might not be possible to preview protected pages and content.
Original Total Estimate:  8  Original FE Estimate:  8  Original DAM Estimate:  0  Original BE Estimate:  0

## Acceptance Criteria
- Contentstack Live Preview SDK is integrated into the metrolinx (next.metrolinx.com) Next.js app router application, enabling real-time preview of draft content entries in the CMS editor.
- A Contentstack Live Preview configuration is added (live_preview hash, enable=true, host, and preview_token) so that editing a draft entry in Contentstack triggers a live preview refresh in the Next.js app.
- Custom preview URLs are configured in Contentstack for at least one representative page template (e.g., a standard content page), so that the preview pane renders the draft entry using the app's rendering pipeline.
- Draft content changes made in the Contentstack editor are reflected in the live preview pane within one revalidation cycle (no manual page refresh required by the author).
- A known-limitation note is documented in the codebase (README or config comment) stating that protected/authenticated pages are excluded from live preview scope.



## Reviewer Feedback — ADDRESS THESE (a prior code review requested changes)
The team-lead reviewer examined your previous attempt and requested the changes below. This is the highest priority.

